A||N||9||Bigfieroman||$500 to spend....on what?||||1||
Z||000000||Bigfieroman||01-11-2001||11:35 AM||||I have $500 to spend on my car, and i was wondering what to spend it on?  I have several routes:<BR>1. Buy brake upgrade, get car painted?<BR>2. Buy lowering eibach springs, bump steer kit, get wheels painted?<BR>3. Buy quater panel vents, window vents, get car painted?<BR>4. Save for 3.4 install?<BR>5. Get stereo, white face gauges, wheels painted?<P>As you can see, i could go on fo a while... but as questions are raised as to the fiero brake upgrade effective ness, my orginal plans of brakes + paint seen to be less appealing...any opinions?<P>------------------<BR>I once got a warning from a Police officer because he couldn't keep up with me around some twisties.  the prerequisite for a warning instead of a ticket was that I must let him drive it back and forth the way we had come.  Burned a quater tank of my gas!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||01-11-2001||11:41 AM||||I'd go for the brake upgrade.  It nice to have a great looking car, but it is necessary to be able to stop the car.  I think any major brake upgrade will be more than $500.||||reg||3
Z||000002||mshill||01-11-2001||11:58 AM||||This comes up quite often.  It seems that $500 is some kinda magic number.  Personally,<BR>I don't think $500 is going to get you a paint job that would last more than a year and look decent at any time other than dusk.<P>Personally, I would put a swaybar on the back (can be done for $50 using a stock front bar of another fiero) and put new OEM brakes (pad, rotors) all around.  Anything left over could go into stereo, gauge faces, etc.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||01-11-2001||12:26 PM||||Start payin back your folks...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Seriously, if I had borrowed from my folks, that would be my ONLY choice. It's good for you that your 'rents are cool about it. If I had an extra $500, first and formost I'd make sure I had the very best tires I could get.  If thats not an issue, I'd go for Koni's.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever2||01-11-2001||01:05 PM||||Find that Christmas Mods thread.  Lots of ideas there.  Like leather seats.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000005||My7Fieros||01-11-2001||03:58 PM||||I could use 500 extra bucks...you can send it to me if you like!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Cliff D.||01-13-2001||09:55 PM||||great call on the tires Stimpy!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Smokin87||01-13-2001||10:29 PM||||im a speed freak. so this is my order of operation, it usually works good. worked for my camaro too.  first, do suspension - that involes copression springs, lowering springs, struts, supports, swaybars, traction bars, and shocks.  then upgrade the brakes.  then that all builds up so when you put a bigger and badder engine in, the car can handle it.||||reg||6
Z||000008||mshill||01-13-2001||11:13 PM||||I'm definitely with stimpy.  I was assuming that was already taken care of.  I speak from experience, one gets a little miffed if someone owes them money and they see that someone spending big bucks before they get paid.||||reg||1
